{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986434-requiem-new-orleans","id":986434,"title":"Requiem New Orleans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-12T15:26:00-07:00","id":986434,"title":"Requiem New Orleans","content":"Other than the obvious issue of Katrina, how do people feel about the New Orleans setting? Do you like it? Dislike it? Is there anything about it you particularly enjoy? Are there any big issues with using it in 2e if you set it during a period prior to Hurricane Katrina?<br /> <br /> Any thoughts are appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:49:37-07:00","id":986472,"title":"","content":"I've run one game with it. Outside of giving the named characters 2nd Edition Stats there isn't much difficult about it (some characters actually worked better with the 2nd Edition Disciplines in my opinion).<br /> <br /> However, I found it felt a bit like a Masquerade &quot;X by Night&quot; book, some of the characters are very Masquerade in style. Overall I prefer the style of the settings in VtR2E.<br /> <br /> I'll get out my notes so I can say something a bit more detailed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T17:14:53-07:00","id":986481,"title":"","content":"I don't have an opinion one way or the other about incorporating Hurricane Katrina. The fact that New Orleans got hit by Hurricane Rita, also one of the worst hurricanes in recorded history just a few weeks after Katrina yet it's completely ignored by the media and how so many people are unaware of that fact is a testament to how selective the news is about accuracy in reporting. Use it or not and move on.<br /> <br /> As far as using the book materials, I thought the Invictus and Carthian Movement were boring and irrelevant except to say they exist in the canon setting.<br /> I liked how it presented how multiple subfactions of the Lancea Sanctum might function. I didn't like how they just aped Roman Catholicism and their only difference was in how much human interaction and ritual observance was considered acceptable by a given faction.<br /> I liked how it showed how the Circle of the Crone would incorporate a polytheistic religion into their beliefs and they got bonus points for not making their NPCs as cliche effete dirt worshipping tree huggers, knockoffs of the characters in the Craft, or misandryst bitches. They lose points for being too patriarchal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-04-2016, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}